{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4k4yz7p54zfrfdaoeohcydqx6pxldogqycj2h4spqqfabolb2mjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the C actually is\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` is `add_executable(driver src/main.c)` — a single 87-line translation unit, **no** CMake options, **no** `#ifdef`s, and `Cargo.toml` had **no** `[features]`. So there is exactly **one** build configuration (documented and swept anyway across debug/release by `check_all_configs.sh`). Because the target is an executable, the public surface is the process boundary plus the TU's only two externally linked symbols, `main` and `run`.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (all in the crate root)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | C external linkage = `{main, run}`; `nm -D` diff **empty** for `.so`↔`.so` and `.so`-equivalent exe symbols; no stubs |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **21 rows**, all `[x]`, derived from the one `return false` (4 distinct conjunct triggers), the ignored `fgets` return, `sizeof(in)==100`, NUL termination, and `printf`'s process-level failures |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **41 config rows** + **4 build rows**, all `[x]`, from 14 branch axes (A–N) read out of the source |\n\nTo make `.so`↔`.so` symbol parity literally exact I added a tiny `ffi/` cdylib member exporting `main` + `run` from the same translated code (a `#[no_mangle] fn main` in an rlib collides with every test harness's entry point, so it needs its own leaf crate).\n\n## Real bug found and fixed\n\n`SIGPIPE`. Rust's runtime installs `SIG_IGN` before `main`; the C inherits the default. With stdout on a dead pipe the C died with signal 13 (status 141) while the Rust exited 0. Fixed by restoring `SIG_DFL` — now both report 141 (rows E17/C34).\n\n## Phases B–D — results\n\n```\ntests/differential_process.rs   37 passed   (C1–C36 + gcc -O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os agreement)\ntests/error_paths.rs            20 passed   (E1–E19, E21)\ntests/ffi_capture.rs             1 passed   (C37–C41/E20, dlopen both .so via libloading)\ntests/symbols.rs                 5 passed   (Phase D parity, RTLD_NOW resolution, no-stub check)\n```\nGreen in **debug and release**, and stable over 15 consecutive full runs. `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings` clean on every target.\n\n## Evidence the tests can actually fail\n\nI mutation-tested the suite. Five of six injected bugs were caught (`saturating_add`, `fgets_line(101)`, `<` vs `<=` on `INT_MAX`, dropped SIGPIPE fix, dropped NUL truncation). The sixth — deleting the `errno == 0` conjunct — is **provably unobservable** on LP64, since `ERANGE` implies `strtol` returned `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN`, which already fail the `INT` range test. That's documented in `ERRORS.md` rather than papered over.\n\nThe harness itself had two bugs the process caught: a race where the child could exit before the pipe's read end closed, and libtest writing its `test … ok` progress lines straight into the fd-1 captures. Both fixed (`run_sequence` now also asserts every captured line has the expected shape, so foreign output can never masquerade as a divergence).\n\nBeyond the suite, 11 498 additional inputs (random bytes, grammar-directed fuzz, length sweeps across the 99-byte `fgets` cut) were compared against the binary from `cmake --build` itself: **0 divergences**. Nothing under `c_src/` was modified — the C artifacts are compiled out of tree into `target/difftest/`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":824,"cache_read_input_tokens":228635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":824,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"256b8717-e7f2-4f66-90f3-0cc283d3f62d","uuid":"b7ddd8db-0e6d-41ba-aed7-2d2e6a26a6c4","timestamp":"2026-08-18T06:08:52.675Z"}
